@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Workspace dependency trees — one table, isolated by copy, installed before the agent

' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, internal/workspace/deps.go,
'         internal/workspace/mount.go, internal/run/run.go,
'         defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh, defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh,
'         defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh, defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh

node "Host checkout" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "source\nbind-mounted at /app" as SRC <<db>>
  database "dependency trees\n""node_modules"" · "".venv"" · ""vendor/bundle""\n""target"" · "".terraform"" · ""lua_modules""" as DEP <<error>>
}

node "proveo run — host side" as RUN <<host>> {
  component "**table** — ""workspace.DepLangs""\nmarkers → dirs, one row per language" as TABLE <<app>>
  component "**plan** — ""MountSpec.DepCopies""\nwalk to depth 4 · one copy per tree, present or not" as PLAN <<app>>
  component "**decide** — ""DepCopyPolicy""\nhost ""GOOS/GOARCH"" vs image ""linux/<arch>""" as POLICY <<app>>
  component "**stage** — ""MaterializeDeps""\ncopy on match · empty on mismatch\n""<state>/egress/<sid>/deps/""" as STAGE <<app>>
}

node "Container — ""proveo_seed"" → ""ensure_dependency_trees""" as C <<host>> {
  component "**discover** — ""_proveo_project_roots""\nsame markers, same depth" as SCAN <<app>>
  component "**classify** — ""_dep_lang_class""\naddons · artifacts · provisioned · portable · none" as CLASS <<app>>
  component "**probe** — ""_proveo_foreign_object""\nELF magic, capped scan" as PROBE <<app>>
  component "**rebuild** — ""_dep_clear_tree"" + ""_dep_install""\nonly where ""_proveo_dep_is_isolated""" as FIX <<app>>
  component "**install** — ""_dep_install""\nabsent → install · native → refresh" as INST <<app>>
}

cloud "Package registry" as REG <<cloud>>
component "Agent" as AGENT <<app>>

TABLE ARROW_MAIN PLAN
PLAN  ARROW_MAIN STAGE : ""DepCopy{Host, Stage, Container}""
POLICY ARROW_MAIN STAGE : reuse? · ""PROVEO_DEPS_COPY"" overrides
DEP   ARROW_OPTIONAL STAGE : plain copy — only when platforms match
STAGE ARROW_MAIN C : mounted rw at ""/app/…/<dir>""
DEP   ARROW_ERROR SRC : never bind-mounted (docker)
SCAN  ARROW_MAIN CLASS
CLASS ARROW_MAIN PROBE : addons · artifacts
PROBE ARROW_MAIN FIX : any non-ELF object
FIX   ARROW_MAIN INST
CLASS ARROW_MAIN INST : portable · absent addons
INST  ARROW_CLOUD REG : lockfile-respecting fetch
INST  ARROW_MAIN AGENT : exec — dependencies in place

note bottom of DEP
  **Not a TypeScript hazard.** ""node_modules"" is the
  loudest instance: gems, luarocks and terraform
  providers all carry host binaries, a venv carries
  the host's interpreter, and build output is stale.
  The remedy is a table, never a special case.
end note

note right of TABLE
  **Two tables, pinned together.** ""DepLangs"" decides
  what the plan hides; ""_dep_lang_dirs"" decides what
  the seed installs into. ""internal/contract"" fails
  the build when they disagree — a tree isolated but
  never installed is an empty overlay the agent trips on.
end note

note bottom of PLAN
  **Pure.** ""Plan"" only NAMES the copies, keyed by
  container path, so ""--print"" renders the real argv
  without copying a tree. ""stageDeps"" (""internal/run"")
  materialises after the backend is chosen and
  removes the stage when the run ends.
end note

note bottom of STAGE
  **Absent on the host is still an overlay.** An empty
  staged dir binds over the would-be path, so the
  install the seed runs lands in the copy — not in a
  Linux ""node_modules"" written into a macOS checkout.
  At a subdir scope's repo root only present trees copy.
end note

note right of POLICY
  **Copy only what can run here.** The defs build
  ""linux/<arch>"" and the runner passes no ""--platform"",
  so the image is linux at the host arch (or
  ""DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM""). A macOS tree is foreign in
  every native module — the seed would clear the copy —
  so a mismatch stages empty and the install is the plan.
end note

note right of FIX
  **A copy may be cleared; the host's tree may not.**
  ""/proc/self/mountinfo"" tells them apart: the copy is
  its own mount point. A package manager keeps the
  foreign binaries it finds, so a rebuild starts empty.
  Host tree: ""PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall"" or ""--clone"".
end note

note right of INST
  **Install first, then the agent.** Absent addons are
  installed; a native tree is refreshed only by managers
  where that is a cheap no-op (""npm ci"" wipes — absent
  or foreign only). A workspace root installs once for
  every member. Lockfiles are respected, never rewritten.
end note

note bottom of REG
  **sbx cannot overlay.** It mirrors the checkout at its
  host path; ""StripDepCopies"" drops the staged dirs and
  the run warns that host trees cross. ""--clone"" carries
  tracked files only, so nothing host-built arrives and
  the seed installs fresh into the clone.
end note
@enduml
